// Standard input asked about before it is read: waiting for a line to
// arrive, and reading it once it has. The input is supplied whole and
// closed, so every wait is answered true and the end of the input is itself
// something to wait for.
//
// The waits have no timeout, so how long the host takes to start watching
// the input doesn't change what they answer. Once the end has been read, a
// wait with a timeout answers at once.

use default

while IO.Std.wait_for_input(0) do
    let line = IO.Std.read_line()

    if !line? then
        break
    fi

    write_line("line: [{line}]")
od

write_line("ended: {IO.Std.wait_for_input(0)} {IO.Std.has_pending_input()}")
write_line("ended, with a timeout: {IO.Std.wait_for_input(1)}")
write_line("heap: {System.GC.get_total_memory(false) > 0L} {System.GC.get_total_memory(true) > 0L}")
